//! The Super AI: a VERA-native decision layer that plays one house through
//! the same [`CommandEnvelope`] stream a human client sends.
//!
//! This is a fork-original feature (not a gamemd port): nothing here traces a
//! native body, and the tiers below describe VERA's own design goals.
//!
//! **Determinism contract.** For an identical simulation view and an identical
//! `tick`, [`SuperAi::orders`] must produce the identical command sequence on
//! every platform and run: the decision layer is a pure function of its
//! arguments plus its own pinned state. The current strategy draws no
//! randomness at all; later milestones that need some must draw from an RNG
//! the instance seeds itself; reading the system clock, global process state
//! or any other ambient source is forbidden. Feeding the returned envelopes
//! to the simulation never mutates the runtime, so the caller can re-derive
//! the same batch at will.
//!
//! **M1 scope.** One deterministic opening: deploy the launch MCV, then walk
//! the side's opening build (power, refinery, barracks, war factory, a second
//! refinery) keeping the building queue busy, place each ready building next
//! to the construction yard, and keep the vehicle queue building harvesters
//! once the war factory stands. From this slice the opening also arms: the
//! vehicle queue keeps miners coming up to a target and then builds the
//! side's main battle tank without pause, the war factory's rally sits on the
//! construction yard so its output gathers in the base, and the barracks
//! queue runs the side's basic soldier continuously. Idle soldiers and tanks
//! defend the base: the nearest intruder inside a ring around the yard draws
//! explicit attack orders, and units with nothing to fight hold an Area
//! Guard post on the yard; a full group gathered there attack-marches on the
//! hostile bases' mass center. Past the opening the construction queue keeps
//! expanding production: a second and third war factory (each extra one
//! multiplies vehicle build time by retail `MultipleFactory=0.8`) with the
//! power plants to feed them, then the tech climb — the radar class and the
//! battle lab, which switches the vehicle queue to the side's tier-2 tank
//! (Prism Tank, Apocalypse, Master Mind). Rallies, guard posts and wave
//! destinations fan out over fixed offsets so groups spread instead of
//! jamming on one cell. Scouting and micro are later milestones; the tiers
//! only change the strength subsidies (opening grant, halved build times),
//! never the decisions themselves.

use vera20k_core::sim::command::Command;
use vera20k_core::sim::command::CommandEnvelope;
use vera20k_core::sim::intern::InternedId;
use vera20k_core::sim::runtime::SimRuntime;

// The difficulty ladder and its Unlimited wallet floor live in
// `sim::driver` beside the policy they map onto, so the engine never
// imports this module (the Phase 1a cycle break). Re-exported unchanged
// for every existing caller of `super_ai::SuperAiDifficulty`.
pub use vera20k_core::sim::driver::{SuperAiDifficulty, UNLIMITED_WALLET_FLOOR};

/// Ticks between two deploy retries: enough for the MCV's deploy animation to
/// finish, few enough to recover within a minute of game time.
const DEPLOY_RETRY_TICKS: u32 = 90;

/// Deploy retries before the opening gives up (a blocked start waypoint will
/// never clear by repeating the order).
const DEPLOY_ATTEMPTS: u8 = 5;

/// How far from the construction yard the site search scans, in cells.
const SITE_SEARCH_RADIUS: i16 = 24;

/// Structures whose foundation owes a clear approach ring: war factories,
/// barracks and naval yards march finished units out of a foundation edge,
/// and a neighbor flush against that edge seals the door — the finished
/// unit wedges inside holding the factory at Done, the queue stops drawing
/// and the whole build chain stalls behind it (observed: a base whose yard
/// had buildings on every side). The site scans demand a two-cell
/// Chebyshev clear ring around these foundations — the conservative form
/// (no per-exit-direction read) — which also carries the one-cell gap
/// every foundation keeps from its neighbors.
const EXIT_CLEARANCE_TYPES: [&str; 9] = [
    "GAWEAP", "NAWEAP", "YAWEAP", // war factories
    "GAPILE", "NAHAND", "YABRCK", // barracks
    "GAYARD", "NAYARD", "YAYARD", // naval yards
];

/// Minimum distance, in cells, from the home yard for an expansion site:
/// anything closer sits inside the home ring-scan's reach, so only the far
/// ore fields — past [`SITE_SEARCH_RADIUS`] — justify walking a base out
/// to them.
const EXPANSION_MIN_DISTANCE: i16 = 30;

/// Deploy attempts the expansion MCV gets before the plan is abandoned —
/// per MCV, unlike the opening's game-lifetime budget, which never sees a
/// later MCV and must not swallow its deploys.
const EXPANSION_DEPLOY_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 5;

/// How far from the expansion yard the sub-base's site search scans, in
/// cells: the engine's own build-area admission (`Adjacent+1` ring, default
/// `Adjacent=3`) already bounds every legal foundation to the yard's
/// neighborhood, so a wider scan would only walk origins the placement
/// order can never land — the scan stays tight and validates each
/// candidate with the engine's real predicate.
const EXPANSION_SITE_RADIUS: i16 = 5;

/// Structures within this many cells of a yard count as that base's
/// cluster: the expansion limbs read the sub-base's power and refinery
/// standing against this ring, and the per-base defense quotas count each
/// yard's guns inside it.
const BASE_CLUSTER_RADIUS: i16 = 8;

/// A standing yard this close (Chebyshev) to the latched far ore field
/// admits the remote-refinery routing around that field: a foundation the
/// scan picks beside a yard-less field sits in no friendly build area and
/// the placement order can never land (observed as OutOfBuildArea
/// rejections soaking the one building slot), so until a yard walked out
/// there the ready refinery takes the home rings or the expansion yard's.
const EXPANSION_YARD_PROXIMITY: i16 = 8;

/// Ore cells within this distance of any standing refinery — any owner's,
/// including other houses' — read as that field's contested half: the ore
/// survey prefers the uncontested fields, so neighboring bases stop
/// latching the same ground.
const ORE_FIELD_EXCLUSION_RADIUS: i16 = 10;

/// The ore survey's enemy-direction bias, a pure tie-break: a candidate
/// field within 5/4 of the home-to-enemy span gains this much score, a
/// field behind home's back loses it. The bias is a tie nudge, never a
/// filter — the survey's richness-per-distance term keeps its voice, and
/// a backward field merely loses ties instead of disappearing (ore
/// direction is not enemy direction, but an outpost that mines at all
/// outranks one that never picked a field).
const ORE_ENEMY_DIRECTION_BIAS: i32 = 1;

/// How many of the fan-out offsets anchor idle defenders around the
/// expansion yard: half the home set, enough posts for the sub-base's
/// guard reserve without thinning the home perimeter's own spread.
const EXPANSION_GUARD_OFFSETS: usize = 8;

/// Miners the vehicle queue builds before it switches to tanks: enough to
/// feed two refineries' docks while the army starts coming out.
const HARVESTER_TARGET: usize = 5;

/// How far from the construction yard an intruder still counts as attacking
/// the base, in cells: the defense picks explicit targets out to this ring;
/// idle units inside it hold an Area Guard post on the yard.
const BASE_DEFENSE_RADIUS: i16 = 16;

/// The base alarm's recency window (Layer 3.5): a building hit this
/// recently — by the house's native damage admission stamp — arms the
/// active-defense limb.
const BASE_ALARM_TICKS: u32 = 90;

/// How long the defense stance holds after its last refresh, in ticks: the
/// defenders keep the focus through the mop-up instead of disbanding the
/// instant the last hit lands.
const DEFENSE_HOLD_TICKS: u32 = 450;

/// The defense stance's commit floor: units are pulled off their guard
/// posts onto the focus until this many defenders stand on it. The
/// [`GUARD_RESERVE`] alone cannot hold a determined push.
const DEFENSE_COMMIT_MIN: usize = 4;

/// The alarm limb's intruder search radius, cells — wider than the idle
/// perimeter's [`BASE_DEFENSE_RADIUS`] so stand-off artillery or a raiding
/// flight sitting outside the perimeter still draws the recall.
const ALARM_RADIUS: i16 = 24;

/// The naval layer (Layer 2.7): combat ships the side fields once its
/// naval yard stands — the basic hull line up to this quota, then the AA
/// escort when its extra prerequisite honestly passes `can_build`.
const NAVAL_SHIP_QUOTA: usize = 3;

/// The second hull line's quota (Layer 2.7): past the basic hull quota the
/// extra hull (the Dolphin, the Giant Squid) rotates up to this many — its
/// own line, not a squeeze on the basic one.
const NAVAL_EXTRA_QUOTA: usize = 3;

/// The capital ship's quota (Layer 2.7): one, behind the battle lab — the
/// Aircraft Carrier and the Dreadnought are the lab's naval expression,
/// and one strike-carrier turns the quota fleet into a siege arm.
const NAVAL_CAPITAL_QUOTA: usize = 1;

/// How far from a yard the naval survey scans for a legal shoreline cell:
/// the naval yard's foundation needs a WaterSet tile inside the base's own
/// build area, so the survey rides the same admission the placement runs.
const NAVAL_SITE_RADIUS: i16 = 14;

/// Pacing between shoreline surveys, in ticks — the ring scan probes a
/// placement per cell, so a landlocked base must not rescan every growth
/// slot.
const NAVAL_PROBE_TICKS: u32 = 900;

/// The survey budget: this many failed probes and the navy is dead for the
/// game (no legal shoreline near any yard).
const NAVAL_PROBE_MAX: u8 = 3;

/// How many standing combat units stay home whatever the offensive does: a
/// base emptied of defenders loses to the first counterattack that walks
/// past the marching wave. A wave forms only while the standing pool
/// outnumbers this reserve, and its picks spend the pool only past it —
/// retail's team scripts never stripped the garrison either.
const GUARD_RESERVE: usize = 4;

/// The infantry that stay home whatever the surplus (W4), on top of
/// [`GUARD_RESERVE`]: the engine parks every fresh infantryman in
/// AreaGuard beside the rally and nothing else ever marched them, so a
/// quota of zero would strip the base's close defense every time a wave
/// forms. Standing combat infantry past reserve plus this quota join the
/// wave as extras instead of hoarding at home.
const HOME_INFANTRY_QUOTA: usize = 6;

/// Power plants the expansion ladder tops out at: each extra war factory
/// drains, and negative power would slow every build through the native
/// power factor in `time_to_build`.
const POWER_TARGET: usize = 3;

/// Standing power plants past which the power limb's next build is a
/// fifth-plus plant — the Soviet Nuclear Reactor override's trigger: with
/// this many Tesla Reactors up and the battle lab standing, the next power
/// want builds one [NANRCT] instead (`Opening::nuclear_reactor`).
const NUCLEAR_OVERRIDE_PLANTS: usize = 4;

/// Refineries the ladder builds before it switches purely to factories:
/// enough docks to keep five miners turning ore into credits.
const REFINERY_TARGET: usize = 2;

/// The assault wave's cadence (retail `TeamDelays=2000` frames): the next
/// wave decision runs this long after the previous episode's launch, and
/// never while that episode still lives — one assault team alive at a
/// time (retail `Max=1`). The interval lets production refill the
/// composition between departures; an episode that outlasts it hands
/// over to the next decision the tick it ends, and a form that never
/// launched re-arms the full interval from its own end.
const WAVE_CADENCE_TICKS: u32 = 2000;

/// The retail gather point (`AISafeDistance`): the cells short of the
/// enemy base the wave regroups at before the strike sequence runs, so the
/// members arrive as one mass instead of single file from the rally.
const WAVE_GATHER_DISTANCE: i16 = 20;

/// Chebyshev cells from the gather cell within which a marched member
/// counts as arrived: every member inside it (or the march clock) turns
/// the march into the strike. One past the march spread's outer reach
/// ([`WAVE_MARCH_SPREAD`] dispatches on the 4-cell ring), so a member the
/// dispatch sent is always a member the arrival read counts.
const WAVE_GATHER_ARRIVAL: i16 = 5;

/// The march dispatch's spread fan (W1): the inner ring of
/// [`SPREAD_OFFSETS`] — the centre and the eight 4-cell offsets. The full
/// table's outer ring marched members 8 cells out, past the arrival read,
/// and the gather clock then disbanded the wave for stragglers it had
/// dispatched there itself (observed: ~1/16 of every wave never counted
/// as arrived, and the clock disbanded most episodes for it).
const WAVE_MARCH_SPREAD: usize = 9;

/// Ticks a forming wave waits for its missing members before it launches
/// with what stands: the composition is a demand, not a precondition — a
/// war-poor base still attacks, with a thinner team, instead of holding
/// its tanks home for the rest of the game.
const WAVE_FORM_TIMEOUT_TICKS: u32 = 1500;

/// The extra forming grace a fresh base alarm buys past
/// [`WAVE_FORM_TIMEOUT_TICKS`]: an alarm may delay the launch, never
/// cancel it. Under constant base alarms the old gate held the forming
/// wave home with no timeout at all (observed: 8275 ticks with zero
/// launches while the army stood complete), so past the form clock plus
/// this grace the thinner wave launches regardless.
const WAVE_ALARM_GRACE_TICKS: u32 = 900;

/// The regroup fraction, as numerator over denominator: this share of the
/// ground members standing inside the arrival ring turns the march. The
/// old all-members rule let one zone-skipped straggler hold the whole
/// wave at the regroup until the march clock ran out (observed: most
/// episodes burned the full clock).
const WAVE_REGROUP_NUMERATOR: usize = 2;
const WAVE_REGROUP_DENOMINATOR: usize = 3;

/// The openness floor a gather cell, a guard post or a congestion
/// discharge cell must pass: at least this many of its eight neighbors
/// still connect in the walker's own zone and hold no structure or
/// terrain object — the choke-avoid test, so a mass never aims at a
/// one-cell pass.
const OPEN_NEIGHBOR_FLOOR: usize = 3;

/// Ticks the march to the gather cell may run before the strike sequence
/// starts regardless: a member engaged on the way, or wedged, must not
/// hold the whole wave at the regroup.
const WAVE_MARCH_TIMEOUT_TICKS: u32 = 1800;

/// Ticks one strike target may hold the wave: past it the episode ends and
/// the members keep whatever attack-move they carry (the engine fights it
/// out), so a target the wave cannot reach never pins the cadence.
const WAVE_STRIKE_TIMEOUT_TICKS: u32 = 3000;

/// Every side's core defense sections — the retail wave script's second
/// quarry (base defenses) after the factories and before the generic
/// buildings: pillboxes, AA towers, heavy towers and the two bunkers.
const WAVE_DEFENSE_TYPES: [&str; 10] = [
    "GAPILL", "NASAM", "ATESLA", "NALASR", "NAFLAK", "TESLA", "YAGGUN", "YAPSYT", "NABNKR",
    "NATBNK",
];

/// Enemy superweapon buildings a wave's strike sequence leads with once
/// they stand revealed (the counter-trigger table's priority strike): the
/// Nuclear Silo and the Weather Controller — the two retail counters name.
const WAVE_LEAD_SUPERWEAPON_TYPES: [&str; 2] = ["NAMISL", "GAWEAT"];

/// Ticks between ore-field re-surveys while the expansion MCV waits: a
/// survey without a deployable winner scans every candidate's
/// neighborhood, so it runs paced, never per tick.
const SURVEY_RETRY_TICKS: u32 = 300;

/// Ticks between two broken-bridge surveys. The survey reads the map's
/// bridge-repair huts and the hostile structures the breach cut off, so it
/// runs paced, never per tick.
const BRIDGE_SURVEY_TICKS: u32 = 200;

/// Ticks before the repair limb may re-issue its capture order or its
/// engineer commission: a dropped [`Command::CaptureBuilding`], or an
/// engineer the queue has not produced yet, must not soak the one-command
/// budget every tick the way an unpaced re-issue once starved the branches
/// below.
const BRIDGE_RETRY_TICKS: u32 = 150;

/// The wallet bar the repair engineer's commission waits for: the commission
/// rides the infantry queue like any unit, so it is only worth a slot while
/// the base's growth is comfortably funded (the air wing's top-up guard, in
/// miniature — a broke base expands, a rich one repairs).
const BRIDGE_ENGINEER_CREDITS: i32 = 2000;

/// Ticks between the building-repair limb's surveys. A survey walks the
/// house's whole structure set (health, repair byte, priority rank), so it
/// runs paced, never per tick; one repair activation at a time latches
/// between surveys anyway.
const REPAIR_SURVEY_TICKS: u32 = 300;

/// The wallet bar a repair activation waits for: repair steps pay as they
/// heal, so a broke base would park a half-paid repair that the engine's
/// own step aborts the moment the wallet dips — the air wing's top-up
/// guard, in miniature. A broke base expands; a funded one repairs.
const STRUCTURE_REPAIR_CREDITS: i32 = 1500;

/// A structure whose health fraction drops under 3/5 earns a repair
/// activation (integer-safe comparison: `health * 5 < strength * 3`).
const REPAIR_FRACTION_NUMERATOR: i32 = 3;
const REPAIR_FRACTION_DENOMINATOR: i32 = 5;

/// The stock bridge-repair hut (retail `BridgeRepairHut=yes`; stock CABHUT
/// is the only one, `object_type.rs`). Resolved through the interner at
/// survey time like every other rules name: a map whose rules lack the type
/// simply skips the limb.
const BRIDGE_HUT_TYPE: &str = "CABHUT";

// The bridge repair's capture infantry is the opening's own `engineer`
// field, not a shared name: the three sides' engineers are three rules
// sections split by `ForbiddenHouses` ([ENGINEER] Allies, [SENGINEER]
// Soviets, [YENGINEER] Yuri), so a shared "ENGINEER" commissioned nobody
// outside an Allied base.

/// Blocker shoves one opening MCV gets while it stands on the same cell:
/// past the cap the site counts as failed and the stuck window below owns
/// the MCV (observed: 582 shove orders across 145 units while one MCV stood
/// at one cell from tick 4000 to 20772, never deploying).
const SHOVE_ATTEMPTS: u32 = 5;

/// Ticks an opening MCV may stand stuck on one cell, refused its deploy
/// spot, before the site is abandoned: a reachable legal foundation is
/// walked to once, or the MCV is latched dead for the deploy branch —
/// anything but shoving forever.
const MCV_STUCK_TICKS: u32 = 600;

/// Cells an opening MCV must travel from its latched site before the
/// per-foundation budgets (deploy attempts, shoves, the stuck window)
/// re-arm: a cell of jiggle must not renew them (the old budget reset
/// re-armed on any movement at all, which is how the shove loop spun).
const MCV_RESITE_DISTANCE: u16 = 4;

/// Every side's war factory type (retail `UIName`s): the structures a wave
/// razes first to starve the enemy's reinforcements.
const WAR_FACTORY_TYPES: [&str; 3] = ["GAWEAP", "NAWEAP", "YAWEAP"];

/// Every side's refinery section name: the ore survey's exclusivity term
/// reads standing structures of any of these — any owner's — so
/// neighboring bases stop latching the same field.
const REFINERY_TYPES: [&str; 3] = ["GAREFN", "NAREFN", "YAREFN"];

/// How long an idle unit that was just given a one-unit order waits before
/// taking another: an order the command layer drops leaves the unit's
/// mission `None`, so without this pause the defense and guard branches
/// would re-order the same first idle unit every tick and starve every
/// branch below them (observed: a Guard post cell blocked by a building
/// froze the whole build ladder for a tank's entire build time).
const IDLE_REORDER_TICKS: u32 = 150;

/// Ticks between the stuck-combat-unit scans: the walk visits every own
/// combat entity, so it runs on this window's pace instead of every tick,
/// like the other unit-wide sweeps' windows.
const STUCK_SCAN_TICKS: u32 = 150;

/// Ticks a combat unit may stand on one cell before the scan re-issues its
/// march: the engine's own pathing burns out to an idle mission when the
/// route exhausts, and nothing above re-orders a mission-less unit whose
/// reorder gate has expired — a wave unit wedged behind a wall stood there
/// for the rest of the game (the [`MCV_STUCK_TICKS`] lesson, for the army
/// instead of the opening MCV).
const STUCK_TIMEOUT: u32 = 600;

/// Units the stuck rescue re-marches per scan, in one pass: the old limb
/// answered one per 150-tick window, so a jam of twenty wedged units took
/// fifty windows to unpick (observed: the 100-unit pileup). Multiple
/// envelopes per tick are the sortie limb's precedent.
const RESCUE_BATCH: usize = 3;

/// Ticks between the congestion scans: the walk snapshots every own
/// ground unit's cell, so it runs on the stuck scan's cadence, never per
/// tick.
const CONGESTION_SCAN_TICKS: u32 = 150;

/// A congestion cluster: at least this many own ground units standing
/// within [`CONGESTION_CLUSTER_RADIUS`] (Chebyshev) of one of them with no
/// displacement over the scan window. The engine's yard-deploy regroup
/// marches every ground unit to one cell and a head-on blocker stops both
/// streams, so a base's whole army piles up on one approach (observed:
/// 100 units frozen on one corridor).
const CONGESTION_CLUSTER_MIN: usize = 8;
const CONGESTION_CLUSTER_RADIUS: i16 = 5;

/// The congestion box's own-house floor (T1): the cluster counts every
/// stationary ground unit of the house and its allies toward
/// [`CONGESTION_CLUSTER_MIN`], but only a box holding at least this many of
/// the house's own is its to unpick — an allied jam two of ours merely
/// stand beside is the ally's own scan's business.
const CONGESTION_OWN_MIN: usize = 3;

/// Cells a congestion centre may drift between two scans and still read
/// as the same standing jam (T2): the cluster's first stationary member
/// shuffles as units scatter, the jam does not.
const CONGESTION_SAME_CENTER: i32 = 3;

/// The persistent jam's attractor reach (T2): a war-factory rally or the
/// wave's gather cell within this many cells of a jam that outlived one
/// scan is what keeps feeding it. Held at the cluster box's own radius,
/// so every jam an attractor proves is also a jam this reach escalates —
/// the old 4 proved jams the 5-wide escalation then never saw.
const CONGESTION_ATTRACTOR_REACH: i32 = CONGESTION_CLUSTER_RADIUS as i32;

/// The home ring the traffic limb does not police (W3): within this many
/// cells of the engine home or an own construction yard a dense standing
/// ring is the base's normal state — the engine parks every new
/// infantryman in AreaGuard beside the rally and the rally itself sits on
/// the offset grid there — so inside it only a wedged unit proves a jam,
/// a jam there holds no march (`jam_on_corridor` measures to the walk's
/// start) and the rescue skips no home-ring unit.
const HOME_JAM_RADIUS: i32 = 12;

/// Ticks a unit the traffic limb moved stays out of its member picks
/// (W3): without it the scan re-fired on the faces it had just parked
/// back into the box — Stop dropped each marcher's AttackMove, the
/// rescue never saw it, and the batches looped every 150 ticks at home
/// (observed: 1846 Stops, 170+ units shuffled five times or more).
/// Pinned map, pruned each scan.
const CONGESTION_MEMBER_COOLDOWN_TICKS: u32 = 600;

/// The yielding house's sidestep (T2): in a jam shared with an ally the
/// smaller house's members walk at least this many cells off the home→jam
/// line, perpendicular to it — clear of the stream both houses feed.
const CONGESTION_YIELD_CLEARANCE: i32 = 4;

/// The jam's blacklist life (T2, T3): a gather cell a jam or the gather
/// clock struck out stays off the gather pick this long, and a rally a jam
/// fed steers clear of that jam's centre for as long.
const TRAFFIC_BLACKLIST_TICKS: u32 = 3000;

/// The openness the wave's gather cell itself must pass (T3) — stricter
/// than [`OPEN_NEIGHBOR_FLOOR`]: a mass regroups on the cell's ring, and a
/// two-wide canyon passes the general floor while it jams a wave.
const GATHER_OPEN_FLOOR: usize = 5;

/// Perpendicular cells a parking cell — a guard post, a hero post, a
/// rally, a repost, a congestion discharge — keeps off the home→enemy axis
/// (T4): the axis is every wave's corridor, and a unit parked on it is the
/// next jam's seed.
const AXIS_CLEARANCE: i32 = 3;

/// The rally bounds (T4): the home factory's rally stays within this many
/// cells of its own yard, the outpost factory's beside the outpost, and a
/// rally a jam fed re-sets at least [`RALLY_JAM_CLEARANCE`] from the jam.
const HOME_RALLY_MAX: i32 = 8;
const OUTPOST_RALLY_MAX: i32 = 6;
const RALLY_JAM_CLEARANCE: i32 = 8;

/// The stuck rescue's first leg (T6): a wedged unit's first rescue walks it
/// to the nearest open cell within this many cells instead of back into
/// the corridor toward the enemy; only a unit wedged again within
/// [`RESCUE_OPEN_RADIUS`] + 2 cells of that first rescue, inside
/// [`RESCUE_MARK_TICKS`] of it, is marched at the enemy.
const RESCUE_OPEN_RADIUS: i32 = 6;
const RESCUE_MARK_TICKS: u32 = 1800;

/// The engine regroup repost (T5): a unit whose destination sits within
/// this many cells of the engine's base centre is regroup-bound, and the
/// re-arm runs at most this long after the yard deploy that fired it.
const REGROUP_REPOST_TOLERANCE: i32 = 6;
const REGROUP_REPOST_WINDOW_TICKS: u32 = 600;

/// The outpost site's allied clearance (T7): a site whose home→site walk
/// passes this close to an allied base centre marches every reinforcement
/// through that ally's yard.
const ALLIED_BASE_CORRIDOR: i32 = 12;

/// The unresolvable strike (T9): an air-sortie target the sorties hit this
/// many cycles without it falling rests off the target list for
/// [`STRIKE_BLACKLIST_TICKS`].
const STRIKE_FUTILE_CYCLES: u32 = 3;
const STRIKE_BLACKLIST_TICKS: u32 = 6000;

/// Ticks a loaded Battle Fortress stands idle before it discharges where
/// it is: the loading pair filled it all game and nothing ever unloaded
/// it (observed: fifteen Enter clicks, zero unloads, the whole match).
const FORTRESS_UNLOAD_IDLE_TICKS: u32 = 300;

/// The farthest an expansion survey may latch a field from home: a site
/// scan with no upper bound walked one owner's MCV ~100 cells into enemy
/// territory and it never deployed (observed).
const EXPANSION_MAX_SITE_DISTANCE: i16 = 70;
/// The outpost siting's hard enemy floor (C2): a field within this many
/// cells of the enemy's standing center is refused outright — the
/// [`enemy_direction_bias`] only nudges ties, and a base that close
/// deploys into the raider's opening walk.
const EXPANSION_ENEMY_FLOOR: i16 = 18;

/// The primary wheel's time arm (Layer 2.9 / outpost P4): past this many
/// ticks since the last toggle the carrier alternates even while the slot
/// odometer stands still, so a quiet factory never pins the flag. It is
/// also the hard floor between two `TogglePrimaryFactory` emissions of one
/// house ([`SuperAi::primary_toggle_due`]): no arm — odometer, demand,
/// first appearance, a lost carrier — may move the flag inside it
/// (observed: 731 toggles at an ~11-tick cadence, home and outpost
/// trading the line under a vehicle re-file storm).
const PRIMARY_TOGGLE_EVERY_TICKS: u32 = 1500;

/// The chrono ride's controllable delay (retail `ChronoDelay=60` frames):
/// the unload after a warp waits this many ticks for the passengers to be
/// ridable again.
const CHRONO_RIDE_DELAY_TICKS: u32 = 60;

/// The Iron Curtain's column: this many of the side's heavy tanks standing
/// inside one 3x3 pad arm the curtain on the pad, and the curtained column
/// then attack-moves at the nearest enemy gun cluster for the curtain's
/// own life (retail 750 frames).
