/// radius from the home center, so a yard-radius read fills the anchor
/// with towers that guard the yard while the corridor the anchor stands
/// on stays naked. Fort guns place on the anchor's own weighted rings
/// ([`PlacementRoute::Fort`]), so everything the anchor arms lands
/// inside this ring.
const DEFENSE_FORT_GUN_RING: i16 = 4;
/// The fort anchors are not structures, so the wall walk keys their ring
/// retirement by this tag packed with the cell — a namespace no entity id
/// reaches.
const DEFENSE_FORT_WALL_KEY: u64 = 0xAAAA_0000_0000_0000;
/// ---- D2 corridor forts: the fort program's unlimited tail. The fort
/// and corridor anchors' guns are money- and grid-gated from here on —
/// no per-anchor quota, no house-wide bound — and the anchors walk out
/// along the approaches the waves actually use.
/// A hostile cluster observed within this many cells of a recorded one
/// refreshes that entry; farther out it opens a new corridor.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_MERGE_RADIUS: i32 = 12;
/// The most corridors the ledger holds; the oldest entry yields when a
/// wider map's waves open more approaches than the program can ladder.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_LEDGER_CAP: usize = 6;
/// Mode B's ceiling on the shared charge: the seat arms
/// [`DefenseStance::SharedObjective`] only while the map's lose-chain
/// objective set holds between one and this many standing objects. Past
/// it the objectives cannot be one ring's charge — the houses would
/// spread thin across the whole map — and mode A's own-lane stance
/// answers better.
pub const DEFENSE_SHARED_OBJECTIVE_CAP: usize = 3;
/// The ladder step: each corridor anchor stands this far past the last,
/// close enough for the stone before it to carry the build area out to
/// it. The step is capped by the ladder stone's own
/// [`vera20k_core::sim::production::build_area_reach_cells`] reach, so a stone
/// queued at one link always stands inside the build area the stone
/// before it carries — the engine's own `Adjacent+1` admission, not a
/// hand-picked spacing. The link before must hold a gun before the next
/// enters, so the chain reaches as far as the wallet ladders it and
/// never queues against ground the build area cannot touch.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_STEP: i32 = 3;
/// The corridor stone (D2-F): the ladder's links are
/// `BaseNormal=no` towers, and a tower carries no build area out —
/// every stone (a retail `BaseNormal=yes` provider) is what carries the
/// engine's `Adjacent+1` ring one link farther (President22's replay:
/// 3011 `outside build area` rejects, every standing tower `bn=false`).
/// The corridor program owes one stone per frontier link before any
/// tower there; the stones queue through the corridor track's own
/// money and pacing gates.
/// A hostile mobile's first crossing of the defended band is an
/// approach when its cell stands within this Chebyshev reach of a fort
/// anchor: the entry ledger ([`DefensePersona::entry_cells`]) records
/// the crossing cell as the corridor ladder's threat target. Sized to
/// the forward interception's reach ([`DEFENSE_INTERCEPT_OUTER_RANGE`]),
/// the band the waves cross on their way in; a sighting beyond it — an
/// enemy garrison standing in its own base — is the enemy's ground, not
/// an approach, and would drag the ladder across the map.
const DEFENSE_ENTRY_RANGE: i32 = 64;
/// The corridor mix rule: one AA gun per this many ground guns at an
/// anchor, and only while the observed-or-scheduled wave carries
/// aircraft — a ground war ladders direct-fire towers alone.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_AA_PER_GROUND: usize = 3;
/// The corridor program's pace: ticks one fort gun past the anchors'
/// floors rests before the next queues. A pace, not a cap — the towers
/// still build without limit — it keeps the growth tail's slots alive
/// between them so a rich wallet ladders the corridor without starving
/// the barracks and factory rungs behind the gun loop.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_GUN_WINDOW: u32 = 450;
/// The corridor track's own pace: the corridor stones and the chain
/// links' towers no longer share the base anchors' gun window above —
/// a base tower's 450-tick rest read as the chain's, and a ladder that
/// may queue one link per 450 ticks never crossed the map in a match
/// (the approaches stayed naked while the wallet was flush). The chain
/// paces itself at this tighter window; each approach's first
/// [`DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_FREE_LINKS`] links and any flush-wallet pass (see
/// [`SuperAi::corridor_pace_flush`]) ride at full speed.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_WINDOW: u32 = 150;
/// Each approach's first links queue without the corridor window: the
/// chain's opening ladder is the difference between a corridor that
/// exists and one that never starts, so the first three climb at full
/// speed and the pace begins past them.
const DEFENSE_CORRIDOR_FREE_LINKS: usize = 3;
/// The defense telemetry's pace: one compact INFO row per adopted
/// defense house every this many ticks — the whole defense posture in a
/// single greppable line (`[DEF-AI]`), so a match's behavior reads from
/// its log without hand-replaying the frame.
const DEFENSE_TELEMETRY_TICKS: u32 = 600;
/// The core's guard fan, sized to the answer it must hold: the standing
/// ±3 hug first, then the same 3-cell lattice's ±6, ±9 and ±12 shells out
/// to the ring spread. An answer wider than one shell stands on the next
/// shell out — the schedule's air answer has posts to hold at the core
/// instead of stalling on nine cells.
fn defense_objective_fan(answer: usize) -> Vec<(i8, i8)> {
    // Two shells out to ±6: a wider fan spread the posts along the wave's
    // approach and the wave ground through them one shell at a time. The
    // objective keeps its guards concentrated; an answer wider than the
    // fan fights from the collapse pool instead of sprawling further.
    const SHELL_STEP: i8 = 3;
    const SHELLS: i8 = 2;
    let shells = SHELLS
        .min(i8::try_from(DEFENSE_OBJECTIVE_RING_SPREAD / i32::from(SHELL_STEP)).unwrap_or(3));
    let mut fan: Vec<(i8, i8)> = Vec::new();
    for shell in 0..=shells {
        for dy in -shell..=shell {
            for dx in -shell..=shell {
                let offset = (dx * SHELL_STEP, dy * SHELL_STEP);
                if !fan.contains(&offset) {
                    fan.push(offset);
                }
            }
        }
        if fan.len() >= answer {
            break;
        }
    }
    fan
}
/// A hostile mobile within this many cells of the nearest protected
/// target — else of the home center — is past the line: a leak.
const DEFENSE_LEAK_RADIUS: i32 = 12;
/// A line unit at or below this health fraction (thousandths) rotates
/// back for repair.
const DEFENSE_REPAIR_FRACTION: i32 = 400;
/// The heal that returns a repaired unit to its post: well above the
/// rotate-out threshold, so a unit parked at the threshold never
